## DESCRIPTION
## Nonlinear systems
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## DBsubject('Calculus - multivariable')
## DBchapter('Differentiation of multivariable functions')
## DBsection('Nonlinear systems')

################################################################

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros("PGstandard.pl", "PGML.pl", "parserRadioButtons.pl");

TEXT(beginproblem());

$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 0;

################################################################
#
#  Setup

$mc1 = RadioButtons(["\( A_1 \neq 0 \)", "\( B_1 \neq 0 \)", "\( C_1 \neq 0 \)", "\( D_1 \neq 0 \)"], "\( C_1 \neq 0 \)");

$mc2 = RadioButtons(["\( C_1 D_2 \neq D_1 C_2 \)", "Insert incorrect answer here", "Insert another incorrect answer here", "Insert yet another incorrect answer here"], "\( C_1 D_2 \neq D_1 C_2 \)");

################################################################
#
#  Text

BEGIN_PGML


Consider the _linear_ maps

>>[` F(w,x,y,z) = A_1w+B_1x+C_1y+D_1z \qquad G(w,x,y,z) =  A_2w+B_2x+C_2y+D_2z `].<<

for fixed constants [` A_1,A_2,B_1,B_2,C_1,C_2,D_1,D_2 \in \mathbb{R} `].

What condition on the constants [` A_1,B_1,C_1,D_1 \in \mathbb{R} `] guarantees that you can solve the equation

>>[` F(w,x,y,z) = 0 `]<<

for [`y`] in terms of [`w,x,`] and [`z`]?

[_]{$mc1}

What condition on the constants [` A_1,A_2,B_1,B_2,C_1,C_2,D_1,D_2 \in \mathbb{R} `] guarantees that you can solve the system of equations

>>[` F(w,x,y,z) = 0, \qquad G(w,x,y,z) = 0 `]<<

for [`y,z`] in terms of [`w,x`]?

[_]{$mc2}
END_PGML

ENDDOCUMENT();